    "lawCode": "Amd R & SS L, generally",
    "lawSection": "Retirement and Social Security Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8584\n\nSPONSOR: JACKSON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the retirement and social security law, in relation to\nproviding certain death benefits to county fire marshals, supervising\nfire marshals, fire marshals, assistant fire marshals, assistant chief\nfire marshals, chief fire marshals and division supervising fire\nmarshals employed by Nassau county\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill provides the death gamble option to Fire Marshals employed by\nNassau County.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends Section 63-g of the Retirement and Social Security Law\nto make technical corrections by updating the titles for Nassau County\nfire marshals.\n\nSection 2 adds a new Section 63-i to the Retirement and Social\n\nSecurity Law to provide Nassau County fire marshals with a death gamble\noption.\n\nSection 3 amends subdivisions (a) and (j) of Section 89-w of the Retire-\nment and Social Security Law to make technical corrections by updating\nthe titles for Nassau County fire marshals.\n\nSection 4 amends subdivision (a) of Section 445 of the Retirement and\nSocial Security Law to make technical corrections by updating the titles\nfor Nassau County fire marshals.\n\nSection 5 adds a new Section 508-c to the Retirement and Social\n\nSecurity Law to provide Nassau County fire marshals with a death gamble\noption.\n\nSection 6 amends subdivision (s) of Section 603 of the Retirement and\nSocial Security Law to make technical corrections by updating the titles\nfor Nassau County fire marshals.\n\nSection 7 amends subdivision (t) of Section 604 of the Retirement and\nSocial Security Law to make technical corrections by updating the titles\nfor Nassau County fire marshals.\n\nSection 8 amends the opening paragraph of subdivision (a) and subdivi-\nsion (g) of Section 605-d of the Retirement and Social\n\nSecurity Law to make technical corrections by updating the titles for\nNassau County fire marshals.\n\nSection 9 amends Section 605-f of the Retirement and Social Security Law\nto make technical corrections by updating the titles for Nassau County\nfire marshals.\n\nSection 10 adds a new Section 606-c to the Retirement and Social\nSecurity Law to provide Nassau County fire marshals with a death gamble\noption.\n\nSection 11 amends subdivision (a) of Section 607-j of the Retirement and\nSocial Security Law to make technical corrections by updating the titles\nfor Nassau County fire marshals.\n\nSection 12 provides that all costs associated with implementing this\nbill shall be borne by Nassau County and may be amortized over a period\nof 10 years.\n\nSection 13 provides that this legislation shall not be subject to the\nappropriation provisions of Section 25 of the Retirement and Social\n\nSecurity Law.\n\nSection 14 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill eliminates any adverse consequences to the beneficiaries of\nNassau County fire marshals who, after being able to file for service\nretirement, decide to continue to serve Nassau County as fire marshals\nand pass away while still being employed as a Nassau County fire\nmarshal. This benefit, known as death gamble, has been available to\nother New York police officers, firefighters, and teachers for over 20\nyears. Death gamble is also currently available to Nassau County deputy\nsheriffs.\n\nThis bill benefits both Nassau County and its residents as well as the\nfamilies of Nassau County fire marshals. This bill allows veteran fire\nmarshals who are entitled to file for service retirement to continue\nserving as fire marshals because any potential adverse consequences\narising from their passing away while employed as a Nassau County fire\nmarshal have been eliminated. Any cost of this bill is outweighed by the\nbenefits to Nassau County, its residents, and the fire marshals.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nSTATE AND LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee fiscal note.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
